      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 29.66,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS ecosystem are used to charge for GPS tracking based on time. Customers pay for tracking by the hour, day, or month, ensuring that they only incur costs when their assets are actively being tracked. This model supports features like pause and resume, allowing users to manage their tracking expenses efficiently.\n\nSource: NAVAS Token Billing Strategy — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
